# Build output
/bin/
/dist/
*.exe

# Go test / coverage artefacts
*.test
*.out
coverage.html

# Local configuration. NEVER commit this: it holds real connection strings and
# passwords. Commit .env.example instead and let each engineer copy it.
.env
.env.local

# Node / Next.js (from Phase 8 onwards)
node_modules/
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo
.pnpm-store/

# Editors and OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json.example

# Local scratch space
/tmp/
/scratch/

# The chart's copy of the pricing catalogue is a BUILD ARTEFACT, produced by `make helm-prepare`.
#
# Helm's .Files.Get can only read inside the chart directory -- a relative path escaping the chart root is
# refused, deliberately, because a chart that read arbitrary host files could not be packaged. So the
# catalogue has to be copied in.
#
# Gitignored rather than committed, because committing it would give two files that drift: the one the CLI
# and `make run-collector` read, and the one the cluster actually uses. One source of truth in git,
# copied at package time.
deploy/helm/kca/catalogue.yaml
